  Slug: choir-politic
  DisplayName: Choir Politic
  IconPath: icons/skills/social/diplomacy-unity-alliance.webp
  Description: "When your patron speaks, it is a chorus of voices sounding as one.
    They first appeared to you in the faces of your neighbors in the middle of a
    town festival or council meeting, when the success of an endeavor hinged on everyone
    working together. With the strength of your patron behind you, you then rallied
    the community together for a common goal. Your patron might be a single entity
    gathering a coterie of subjects together for an unknown cause or a like-minded
    covenant of deities and spirits. Whatever the case, your patron\u2014and by extension,
    you\u2014understands that mortals are stronger together. Spell List divine Patron
    Skill Religion Lesson of Community Knowledge Your patron taught you the importance
    of pooling information to help a group with a common cause. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Share
    Vision] hex cantrip and your familiar learns @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Share
    Lore]. Familiar of Bolstering Aid Your familiar knows all manner of tricks that
    can help! When you Cast or Sustain a hex, and your familiar is adjacent to an
    ally, that ally gains a +2 status bonus to the next non-attack skill check that
    ally attempts before the start of your next turn."
